          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us learn more about these stages in the life cycle of a mosquito."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.124,
            0.743,
            0.166
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Mosquitoes pass through four stages in their life cycle— egg, larva, pupa and adult (Fig. 10.6)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.166,
            0.744,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The adult mosquito that emerges from the pupa rests briefly on the surface of water and then flies away. The adult mosquito may survive for 10 to 15 days."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.227,
            0.744,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have seen that a mosquito begins its life as an egg (stage I), the egg develops into a larva (stage II), the larva grows into pupa (stage III), and the pupa transforms into an adult mosquito (stage IV). The adult female mosquito lays eggs directly on or near water, and the cycle continues."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.329,
            0.746,
            0.455
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Significant changes occur in the appearance, body shape and structure during the various stages in the life cycle of a mosquito. The shape of the egg is quite different from the larva; the larva appears very different from the pupa. The pupa appears very distinct from the adult mosquito. Is it easy to imagine that a mosquito emerges from a pupa?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.482,
            0.745,
            0.629
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The silk moth also passes through four life stages—egg, larva, pupa and adult. Eggs hatch into larvae, which then grow in size. Larvae secrete thread-like material which they wrap around themselves, before changing to pupae. These are the fibres that are used to make silk fabric. In India, the Khadi and Village Industries Commission (KVIC) has set up several centres for silk production. ou Do y"
            }
          ]
        },
